# Production deliverables produced by `python hardware/kicad/build.py`.
#
# Vendor-isolated layout: each fabricator gets its own subdirectory under
# `output/`. Each subdirectory carries EXACTLY 4 committed files.
#
# Currently shipping:
#   jlcpcb/oas-jlcpcb.zip       Gerbers + Excellon drill bundle (bare board)
#   jlcpcb/oas-BOM.csv          BOM (JLCPCB template + LCSC# + library tier)
#   jlcpcb/oas-top-CPL.csv      CPL top (Designator, Mid X, Mid Y, Layer, Rotation)
#   jlcpcb/oas-bottom-CPL.csv   CPL bottom (empty — no bottom-side SMD on OAS)
#
# Intermediate raw fab data (Protel gerbers + Excellon + drill_map PDFs) is
# regenerable but NOT committed — see `hardware/build/gerbers/` (gitignored
# via the generic `**/build/` rule). Stage 20 of `build.py` writes those;
# stage 32 zips them into `jlcpcb/oas-jlcpcb.zip`.
#
# JLCPCB upload: oas-jlcpcb.zip for the bare board, then oas-top-CPL.csv +
# oas-BOM.csv on the SMT quote page (Parts Selection = "By Customer").
